    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46958" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠμάτιος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦμαρ</span>) poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμερήσιος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>by day</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠματίη μὲν δφαίνεσκεν μέγαν ἱστόν,
					νύκτας δ᾽ ἀλλύεσκεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.104
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				19.149
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠμάτιαι σπεύδουσι
			[μέλισσαι</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				597
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠ. φέγγος</span>, i.e. the sun, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.651
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>day by day, daily</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.72
			</span></i>.</div>
